--- !u!114 &146502576
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 146502574}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 558c1484d7e2c4d2b9b027dfe470ea0a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::StorySequenceController
  introVideoPanel: {fileID: 0}
  mainCamera: {fileID: 993644470}
  dialoguePanel: {fileID: 1102184500}
  speakerText: {fileID: 505338093}
  bodyText: {fileID: 109741875}
  playerObject: {fileID: 2003422652}
  npcObjects:
  - {fileID: 1225850042}
  beforeItemsSteps:
  - stepLabel: CUT SCENE 0
    videoPanel: {fileID: 0}
    cutscene: {fileID: 2112371203}
    cameraAnchor: {fileID: 0}
    dialogueLines: []
  - stepLabel: 'CUT SCENE 1 '
    videoPanel: {fileID: 0}
    cutscene: {fileID: 973243514}
    cameraAnchor: {fileID: 659440768}
    dialogueLines:
    - speaker: MOTHER
      text: Ely, gumising ka na Ely! Umuulan na, kailangan natin tumakas dito.
    - speaker: ELY
      text: Okay Ma. Lord bat ngayon pa? Kakaayos lang namin ng bahay kahapon.
    - speaker: MOTHER
      text: Naghihintay na yung tatay mo at yung kapatid mo sa labas. Bilisan mo na 'nak.
    - speaker: ELY
      text: Sige po ma. Ang layo pa ng evacuation center, aabutan ba namin? Sana nga.
    - speaker: ELY
      text: e
  - stepLabel: CUT SCENE 2
    videoPanel: {fileID: 0}
    cutscene: {fileID: 1713737570}
    cameraAnchor: {fileID: 659440768}
    dialogueLines:
    - speaker: ELY
      text: This is Ely Payong, a child living below the poverty line with his family.
    - speaker: ELY
      text: His mother and his father used to work at their own bakery. Theirs was a business beloved by the community.
    - speaker: ELY
      text: Until one day, El Nino came, and swept their lives, along with many others, away.
    - speaker: ELY
      text: Now, Ely and his family live in the destroyed forest outside of the city. They never recovered from the destruction on that day. Some blame nature taking its course, others blame a lack of foresight from the people.
    - speaker: ELY
      text: Ely however, blames the government, and not without good reason. They cut down the forest, their natural barrier from the flooding, and without it, the destruction followed.
  - stepLabel: CUT SCENE 3
    videoPanel: {fileID: 0}
    cutscene: {fileID: 420347768}
    cameraAnchor: {fileID: 1970289073}
    dialogueLines:
    - speaker: Mother
      text: Kunin mo yung tubig Ely, malay mo kung masira yung planta ngayon.
    - speaker: ELY
      text: Sige po ma.
    - speaker: ELY
      text: The only bone that the government has ever thrown their community is the water treatment plant, and even that is privately owned.
    - speaker: ELY
      text: Come every flood, every disaster, the plant has always worked and provided clean drinking water and bathing water during times of crisis. Ironically, the only time Ely and his family get to enjoy those luxuries is when they're in the evacuation center.
  itemsRequired: 2
  afterItemsSteps:
  - stepLabel: Cut Scene 4
    videoPanel: {fileID: 0}
    cutscene: {fileID: 667371658}
    cameraAnchor: {fileID: 1970289073}
    dialogueLines:
    - speaker: Mother
      text: AY! Ayun na lumulubog na naman ulet yung gubatan, blisin mo na 'nak!
    - speaker: ELY
      text: Nagmamadali na po ako ma!
    - speaker: ELY
      text: The rain started falling like arrows onto their rooftop. The streets were flooded in ankle-high water, mixed with the filth left behind by inconsiderate visitors, and the dead foliage that came to rest on the forest floor.
    - speaker: Mother
      text: ELY! Bilisan mo na!
    - speaker: ELY
      text: Ito na nga ma!
  - stepLabel: Cut Scene 5
    videoPanel: {fileID: 0}
    cutscene: {fileID: 2025079451}
    cameraAnchor: {fileID: 1970289073}
    dialogueLines: []
  nextSceneName: Area1
